    "q": "Unexplained dizziness with different blood pressures in the arms suggests which steal syndrome? What additional bedside measurement helps if only one arm pressure is given?",
    "a": "Subclavian steal syndrome from reversed vertebral-artery flow. Check blood pressure in the other arm; CT or MR angiography can establish the diagnosis.",
