    "q": "A patient has stroke-like symptoms with ipsilateral neck or facial pain. Which arterial pathology is described?",
    "a": "Carotid artery dissection. Pain reflects stretching of vascular nociceptors; thrombus within the false lumen can embolize to the brain or eye.",
